		(uuid "a2d6e9f6-e774-4658-8ff5-93a033c51f52")
	)
	(text "INA226: I2C address 0x40 (A0 = A1 = GND), alert on GPIO7, VS = 3.3 V.\nR23 2 mOhm: +-41 A full scale, 1.25 mA resolution, 0.34 W at 13 A.\nKelvin-connect Vin+ / Vin- right at the R23 pads. +24V / MOTOR_24V / MOTOR_SW:\ncopper for 15 A (pours, or >= 5 mm in 1 oz)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 265.43 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a935856b-87ff-4829-b8dd-1daa0b50b38f")
	)
	(text "Ceramic output compensation (TI SLVA237):\nL1 22 uH, C7 + C8 2 x 47 uF: f_LC ~ 4.7 kHz.\nC4 / R9 / C12 / C11: crossover 14-27 kHz,\nphase margin > 60 deg, 0.1 to 1.5 A."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 135.382 83.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "ccb79025-7eaa-4393-9794-6da36b2edd78")
	)
	(text "R14 / R17: bias.  R16 (DNP): 120R termination,\nonly for cords over ~5 m (then R14 / R17 = 680R)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 336.55 160.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d03d16bd-0e08-4ff9-8320-ec47a0507bfd")
	)
	(text "ENA left open: internal 1.5 MOhm pull-up"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 26.416 76.962 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "d1d23275-8ef9-4a2b-b4f5-9bafe6a76f3d")
	)
	(text "PH = DIR, EN = PWM. EN low = brake (both low sides on).\nnSLEEP low = FETs held off; its internal 115k pull-down\nkeeps the bridge off during a reset or the bootloader.\nFirmware: nSLEEP high once MOTOR_SW is up, PWM 1 ms\nlater; nFAULT: MCU pull-up on.\n\nCurrent limit, cycle by cycle: R27 + R28 = 4 mOhm in\nthe low-side return (LS_SRC), Kelvin taps to SP / SN.\nVREF = 5 V x 3.3k / 13.3k = 1.22 V (+5V: tighter than\nAVDD, 4.4-5.2 V). ICHOP = (VREF - VOFF) / (20 x 4 mOhm)\n= 14.6 A typ. with VOFF = 50 mV; 9.5 to 18 A worst case\n(VOFF up to 250 mV, gain 18-24). Above ICHOP the bridge\nbrakes for 25 us, then drives again. R30 = 4.7k: 19 A.\nTP14 = SO = VOFF + 80 mV/A while driving; SO = VOFF\nwhen the bridge is awake and stopped.\nThe INA226 still measures the supply current and cuts\nthe PWM and Q5. The DRV8701 also trips at 1 V VDS.\n\nJ7: 7.62 mm pluggable header, so the 5.08 mm 24 V plug\nof J1 / J5 cannot go into the motor output.\nIDRIVE open: 100 mA source / 200 mA sink.\nBypass with an external driver on J5 / J6: cut JP2-JP5\nand the JP6 wire link (1.5 mm2, hand-soldered)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 180.34 211.455 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dc4f551e-2010-4ef0-a076-36d4476414ac")
	)
